1.ARRAY SEARCH
Given an array, arr[] of n integers, and an integer element x, find whether element x is present in the array. 
Return the index of the first occurrence of x in the array, or -1 if it doesn't exist.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int search(int arr[], int x) {
                int n=arr.length;
                for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {
                    if(arr[i]==x) {
                        return i;
                    }
                }
                return -1;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/search-an-element-in-an-array-1587115621/1


2.MINIMUM PRODUCT OF K ELEMENTS
Given an array arr of positive integers, return the minimum possible product of any k elements from the array. Return the result modulo 1e9 + 7.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            int minProduct(int arr[], int k) {
                long mod=1000000007L;
                if(k>arr.length){
                    k=arr.length;
                }
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                long product=1;
                for(int i=0;i<k;i++){
                    product=(product*arr[i])%mod;
                }
                return (int) product;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/minimum-product-of-k-integers2553/1


3.MAXIMUM TRIPLETS SUM IN ARRAY
Given an array arr, the task is to find the maximum triplet sum in the array.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public int maxTripletSum(List<Integer> arr) {
                Collections.sort(arr);
                int n=arr.size();
                return (arr.get(n-1)+arr.get(n-2)+arr.get(n-3));
            }
        }
